      "text": "Given the expression \\((3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\\), we can use the distributive property to expand it:\n\n\\[\n(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x) = 3x^2 \\cdot 7 + 3x^2 \\cdot (-2x) + (-5x) \\cdot 7 + (-5x) \\cdot (-2x) + 4 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot (-2x)\n\\]\n\nSimplify each term:\n\n\\[\n= 21x^2 - 6x^3 - 35x + 10x^2 + 28 - 8x\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\n\\[\n-6x^3 + (21x^2 + 10x^2) + (-35x - 8x) + 28\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= -6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28\n\\]\n\nThe expression \\( -6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28 \\) can be written in the form \\( ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d \\) where \\( a = -6 \\), \\( b = 31 \\), \\( c = -43 \\), and \\( d = 28 \\).\n\nNow we need to find \\( 8a + 4b + 2c + d \\):\n\n\\[\n8a + 4b + 2c + d = 8(-6) + 4(31) + 2(-43) + 28\n\\]\n\nCalculate step by step:\n\n\\[\n= 8(-6) + 4(31) + 2(-43) + 28\n\\]\n\nFirst,\n\\[\n8(-6) = -48\n\\]\n\\[\n4(31) = 124\n\\]\n\\[\n2(-43) = -86\n\\]\n\nCombine these terms and add \\( 28 \\):\n\n\\[\n-48 + 124 - 86 + 28\n\\]\n\nStep-by-step calculation:\n\n1. Combine \\(-48 + 124\\):\n\\[\n-48 + 124 = 72\n\\]\n\n2. Combine \\( 72 - 86 \\):\n\\[\n72 - 86 = -14\n\\]\n\n3. Combine \\(-14 + 28\\):\n\\[ -14 + 28 = 14 \\]\n\nTherefore, the final expression is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{14}\n\\]",
